    "preview": "# Knowledge Guide for California Schools Database\n\n## 1. Introduction\nThis guide serves as a comprehensive semantic layer for the `california_schools` database, providing a unified understanding of its structure, key entities, and business metrics. It is designed to support enterprise-level data governance, ensuring consistency, accuracy, and clarity in data usage across various business contexts.\n\n## 2. Core Entities & Fields\n\n### Schools\n- **CDSCode (text):** Unique identifier for each school.\n- **School Name (text):** Official name of the school.\n- **County (text):** Name of the county where the school is located.\n- **District (text):** Name of the school district.\n- **Street, City, State, Zip (text):** Full physical address of the school.\n- **Phone (text):** Contact number for the school.\n- **OpenDate, ClosedDate (date):** Dates indicating when the school was opened or closed.\n- **Charter (integer):** Indicates if the school is a charter school (1 for yes, 0 for no).\n- **Virtual (text):** Indicates if the school offers virtual instruction ('F' for exclusively virtual).\n\n### Enrollment & Meals\n- **Enrollment (K-12) (real):** Total number of students enrolled in grades K-12.\n- **Enrollment (Ages 5-17) (real):** Total number of students aged 5-17.\n- **Free Meal Count (K-12) (real):** Number of students in K-12 eligible for free meals.\n- **Free Meal Count (Ages 5-17) (real):** Number of students aged 5-17 eligible for free meals.\n\n### SAT Scores\n- **Average Scores in Math, Reading, Writing (integer):** Average SAT scores in respective subjects.\n- **Number of Test Takers (integer):** Total number of students who took the SAT.\n- **NumGE1500 (integer):** Number of students with SAT scores greater than or equal to 1500.\n\n## 3. Metric Definitions\n\n### Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)\n- **Total Enrollment:** `Enrollment (K-12)` + `Enrollment (Ages 5-17)`\n- **Excellence Rate:** `NumGE1500 / Number of Test Takers`\n- **Eligible Free Rate (K-12):** `Free Meal Count (K-12) / Enrollment (K-12)`\n- **Eligible Free Rate (Ages 5-17):** `Free Meal Count (Ages 5-17) / Enrollment (Ages 5-17)`\n\n### Business Metrics\n- **Difference in Enrollment:** `Enrollment (K-12)` - `Enrollment (Ages 5-17)`\n- **Percent Eligible for Free Meals (K-12):** `(Free Meal Count (K-12) / Enrollment (K-12)) * 100`\n- **Percent Eligible for Free Meals (Ages 5-17):** `(Free Meal Count (Ages 5-17) / Enrollment (Ages 5-17)) * 100`\n\n## 4. Constraints & Conventions\n\n### Filtering Criteria\n- **Virtual Schools:** Filter using `Virtual = 'F'` for exclusively virtual schools.\n- **Charter Schools:** Use `Charter = 1` to identify charter schools.\n\n### Temporal Boundaries\n- **Fiscal Year Format:** Use the academic year format (e.g., 2022-2023) for temporal analysis.\n\n### Unit Conversions\n- **Percentage Calculations:** Ensure all percentage metrics are multiplied by 100 for clarity.\n\n## 5. Exemplar Use Cases\n\n### Example 1: Calculating Total Enrollment\n- **Metric:** Total Enrollment\n- **SQL Logic:** `SELECT T2.CDSCode, (T2.\"Enrollment (K-12)\" + T2.\"Enrollment (Ages 5-17)\") AS TotalEnrollment FROM frpm AS T2`\n- **Explanation:** This query calculates the total enrollment by summing the K-12 and ages 5-17 enrollments for each school.\n\n### Example 2: Identifying Schools with High Excellence Rate\n- **Metric:** Excellence Rate > 0.3\n- **SQL Logic:** `SELECT T1.CDSCode FROM satscores AS T1 WHERE (T1.NumGE1500 / T1.NumTstTakr) > 0.3`\n- **Explanation:** This identifies schools where more than 30% of test takers scored 1500 or above on the SAT.\n\n### Example 3: Schools with High Free Meal Eligibility\n- **Metric:** Percent Eligible for Free Meals (K-12) > 10%\n- **SQL Logic:** `SELECT T2.CDSCode FROM frpm AS T2 WHERE (T2.\"Free Meal Count (K-12)\" / T2.\"Enrollment (K-12)\") > 0.1`\n- **Explanation:** This identifies schools where more than 10% of K-12 students are eligible for free meals.\n\n### Example 4: Ranking Schools by Writing Scores\n- **Metric:** Average Writing Score > 499\n- **SQL Logic:** `SELE",
